        // However, to make it a general fuzz test, we need the fuzzer to find a case where
        // the return value differs. Since we can't fuzz the immutable args, we'll fuzz
        // the expectedOwner parameter and assert that owner() is NOT equal to the bug constant,
        // because in the reference, owner() will return the actual owner from calldata
        // (which is unlikely to be 0x000...001), so the assertion passes for all inputs.
        // In the buggy version, owner() always returns 0x000...001, so the assertion fails
        // for any expectedOwner not equal to that constant.
        assertTrue(c.owner() != address(0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000001) || expectedOwner == address(0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000001));
    }
}

